1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,895
Layered Spring apps often still let the
framework sit in the middle of the onion.

2
00:00:05,016 --> 00:00:15,984
A “domain” class annotated with JPA and
Jackson, a service that returns
ResponseEntity, a repository interface
that extends Spring Data in the same
package as release rules — the layers have
names,

3
00:00:16,103 --> 00:00:18,936
but the center is not isolated.

4
00:00:19,055 --> 00:00:32,447
Hexagonal architecture — ports and
adapters — flips the gravity for gate
release: the domain sits in the center;
HTTP, billing Feign, and JPA plug in
around it. Alistair Cockburn’s idea is
concrete here.

5
00:00:32,567 --> 00:00:43,991
The application core defines ports —
interfaces for what drives gate release
and what release needs. Adapters implement
those ports. The core never imports Spring
Web.

6
00:00:44,111 --> 00:00:55,703
Boot remains the composition root that
wires adapters to ports. Draw one hexagon
for gate release: - Driving (primary)
port: ReleaseGateUseCase — what the booth
can ask the app to do.

7
00:00:55,823 --> 00:01:10,128
- Driven (secondary) ports: GateLedger,
BillingPort — what release needs from the
outside. - Adapters: GateController (MVC)
drives the use case; JpaGateLedgerAdapter
and BillingFeignAdapter implement driven
ports.

8
00:01:10,247 --> 00:01:25,463
Look at this java for a moment. Look at
this java for a moment. Look at this java
for a moment. Unit tests construct
ReleaseGateService with fake BillingPort
and GateLedger — no MockMvc required for
tariff branching.

9
00:01:25,583 --> 00:01:39,791
Slice tests cover the MVC adapter.
Production wiring is a @Configuration that
binds interfaces to adapters. The hexagon
is not a folder religion; it is dependency
direction you can point at in review.

10
00:01:39,911 --> 00:01:51,383
A misconception is drawing hexagons in
Confluence while controllers still call
Feign clients directly. Another is ports
for every trivial getter until the core is
an interface museum.

11
00:01:51,503 --> 00:01:58,223
A third is putting Spring Data interfaces
in the domain package and declaring
victory because the folder says domain.

12
00:01:58,343 --> 00:02:11,183
Hexagonal’s cousin names the same gravity
with rings and an explicit dependency
rule: source code dependencies point only
inward. That formulation is Clean
Architecture — and it sharpens what the
gate domain may import.
